<title>FINLAND: GERMANY'S SIEMENS COMMITTED TO LITHUANIA.</title>
<headline>GERMANY'S SIEMENS COMMITTED TO LITHUANIA.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German industrial group Siemens does not plan to quit Lithuania despite comments by local company representatives it wants to leave the Baltic state.</p>
<p>A Siemens company official was quoted as saying recently that the Lithuanian litas was over-valued and that Siemens was considering quitting the country.</p>
<p>But a company official at an investment conference here said that Siemens planned to stay.</p>
<p>&quot;We are committed to being there and we are comitted to investing more,&quot; Jukka Pertola, a director of Siemens private communications systems, told Reuters.</p>
<p>-- Patrick Lannin, Helsinki +371 9 356 187</p>
</text>
